WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.400
Bridgecall connects a reviewed knowledge base, localized conversation flows, and live coaching. This

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.800
walkthrough uses synthetic narration. The application screenshots are actual captures. The evidence

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:22.200
distinguishes generated audio, real time audio processing, and recordings of real people.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.148
One design choice is returning approved passages directly, instead of generating new financial

00:00:29.148 --> 00:00:35.496
product claims. Each supported answer has a source reference. Unsupported questions receive a

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:41.844
fallback. A state machine keeps consent separate from qualification. This makes the prototype easy

00:00:41.844 --> 00:00:48.192
to inspect, with the tradeoff of narrow paraphrase handling.

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:55.638
Audio testing found a concrete failure. The recognizer expanded W I B into waktu Indonesia Barat.

00:00:55.638 --> 00:01:02.484
The callback parser accepted the abbreviation but rejected the spoken phrase. The parser now accepts

00:01:02.484 --> 00:01:09.330
the three spoken Indonesian timezone names. Regression tests check that confirmation is still

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.176
required. Original failed audio and corrected reruns are both retained.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:23.790
The companion live demo plays synthetic speech at real time speed. Every four second window passes

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:30.804
through local Whisper before the browser displays a nudge. End to end latency was four point nine

00:01:30.804 --> 00:01:37.818
one seconds at the median, and eight point seven three seconds at the ninety fifth percentile, over

00:01:37.818 --> 00:01:44.832
ten windows. The capture interval is included. No language model is used for the nudge rules.

00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:51.828
Five expected signals were detected, one was missed, and four negative windows produced no alert.

00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:58.224
The missed signal came from hearing cannot pay as cannot be. Short Filipino consent words were also

00:01:58.224 --> 00:02:04.620
unreliable. The system keeps ambiguous speech out of the consent path. These are small authored

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:11.016
tests, not claims of production accuracy.

00:02:11.616 --> 00:02:17.525
For a regional accent test, local Whisper transcribed published Indonesian news recordings: one

00:02:17.525 --> 00:02:23.434
Javanese accented speaker and one standard speaker, reading three matched sentences each. Word error

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:29.342
rates were twenty eight point six and thirty two point one percent. This tiny sample cannot

00:02:29.342 --> 00:02:35.251
establish an accent ranking. The report links the original source and does not redistribute its

00:02:35.251 --> 00:02:41.160
recordings.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.882
Start with the audio evidence report in the repository. It links seven synthetic dialogue

00:02:48.882 --> 00:02:56.004
recordings, the corrected Indonesian reruns, the live screen capture, and the regional accent

00:02:56.004 --> 00:03:03.126
results. Remaining work includes real interactive calls, native speaker review, stronger Filipino

00:03:03.126 --> 00:03:10.248
recognition, and deployment hardening. The business data is fictional and callbacks are local mocks.
